From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:10:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 366/366] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: enable the keyboard
 ghost filter

The Gemini PDA keyboard matrix has no per-key diodes. The vendor driver
explicitly blocks ghosted positions, and its comment says Ctrl+Left
Shift+N also reads M. That is the fourth corner of the rectangle formed
by LeftCtrl (4,6), LeftShift (3,6) and N (3,2) in this map.

Mark the matrix with needs-ghost-filter so ambiguous scans are dropped
instead of reporting a phantom key.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
index 96528e66b..337aac1d5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -469,6 +469,8 @@ keyboard-matrix {
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		gpio-activelow;
 		drive-inactive-cols;
+		/* No per-key diodes: Ctrl+Left Shift+N also reads M. */
+		needs-ghost-filter;
 		pinctrl-0 = <&keyboard_matrix_row_pins
 				     &keyboard_matrix_col_pins>;
 		row-gpios = <&aw9523 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>,
